**What it shows:** If base class functions are not `virtual`, derived overrides are ignored when called through a base reference — causing wrong behavior (e.g., expecting 'P' but showing 'C'). Making the base function `virtual` fixes it. This follows the PassFailActivity example & Program 15-10/15-11 in your slides. fileciteturn0file0

