# **TOPIC 1 — Basic Inheritance (Base → Derived)**  
**(Ref: Your PDF section on “Basic Inheritance” introduction)** fileciteturn0file0

---

## **THEORY — What Actually Happens**
Inheritance = reuse + extend.  
A derived class **inherits all members** of a base class except constructors/destructors and private items.

Think of it like:

```
BaseClass
   ↑
   |
DerivedClass   (Derived = Base + More)
```

Key rules:
1. Base part is always created **first**.
2. Derived part is destroyed **first**.
3. Private data of base cannot be directly accessed in derived.
4. Public & protected of base are accessible depending on mode (public/protected/private inheritance).

---

## **CODE — Clean Runnable Example**

```cpp
// t1_basic_inheritance.cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

class Base {
public:
    int x;
    void showBase() {
        cout << "Base x = " << x << "\n";
    }
};

class Derived : public Base {   // PUBLIC INHERITANCE
public:
    int y;
    void showDerived() {
        cout << "Derived y = " << y << "\n";
    }
};

int main() {
    Derived d;
    d.x = 10;   // inherited
    d.y = 20;   // own member

    d.showBase();
    d.showDerived();
}
```

**Expected Output**
```
Base x = 10
Derived y = 20
```

