# ⭐ Why use interfaces?

- Force a common behavior  
- Allow different classes to behave uniformly  
- Useful in polymorphic collections

Example:

```
Printable* arr[3];
arr[0] = new Invoice;
arr[1] = new Report;
arr[2] = new Card;

arr[i]->print();   // each prints differently
```

