# ⭐ **TOPIC 8 — Virtual Destructors**  
(This is very important when deleting derived objects through base pointers.)

---

# 🎯 Why needed?

If base destructor is **NOT** virtual:

```cpp
Base* p = new Derived;
delete p;
```

Only Base destructor runs → Derived destructor **never** runs → memory leak.

---

# ⭐ FIX:

```cpp
class Base {
public:
    virtual ~Base() { }
};
```

Now deleting through base pointer calls destruction properly.

---

# ⭐ Super Easy Example

```cpp
class Base {
public:
    virtual ~Base() { cout << "Base destroyed\n"; }
};

class Derived : public Base {
public:
    ~Derived() { cout << "Derived destroyed\n"; }
};

int main() {
    Base *p = new Derived;
    delete p;
}
```

**Output**
```
Derived destroyed
Base destroyed
```

This proves virtual destructor worked.

